C o m p i l a t i o n


      CEE 6410 - HW 6
            Example 7.1 in the Bishop et al text
             
            
   7  Sets src    Which source the water is coming from /res "Reservoir", pump "Pump"/
   8       seas   Seaon 1 or season 2 /s1*s2/
   9       cap    Storage in the Reserovoir /cap0, cap1, cap2/;
  10   
  11   
  12  Variables I(src, cap)  Decision to build_use source (1=do 0=don't)
  13            V(src, seas) Volume of water to take from each source (ac-ft)
  14            Stor(seas)   How much volume to store in Reservoir (ac-ft)
  15            Flow(seas)   How much volume to relea from river
  16            Area         How much area to irrigate
  17            TotalBen       Maximum benefit from both sources;
  18   
  19  Binary Variables I;
  20   
  21  Positive Variables V, Flow, Stor;
  22   
  23   
  24  Table CostCap(src, cap) Capital cost to build projects ($ per year))
  25                cap0   cap1    cap2
  26        res      0     6000    10000
  27        pump     0     8000    8000;
  28   
  29   
  30  Parameter CostOpr(src)  Operating Cost of each source ($ per ac-ft)
  31         /res    0,
  32         pump    20/ ;
  33   
  34  Table MaxCap(src, cap) Maximum capacity built (ac-ft per season)
  35             cap0   cap1   cap2
  36       res    0     300    700;
  37   
  38   
  39  MaxCap("pump","cap1") = 2.2*365/card(seas);
  40   
  41  Parameters Inflow(seas) River inflow per season (ac-ft)
  42                     /s1 600, s2 200/
  43             Demand(seas) Irrigation demand in time t (ac-ft per acre)
  44                     /s1 1.0, s2 3.0/
  45             BaseFlow River baseflow below the reservoir (ac-ft) /730/
  46             Rev      Revenue of irrigation ($ per year per acre) /300/;
  47   
  48   
  49   
  50  Equations
  51      SupplyArea(seas)    How much area to supply (ac)
  52      NetBen              Objective Function Revenue minus costs
  53      PumpCap(seas)       Pumping in each season (ac-ft per season)
  54      ResCap(seas)        Reservoir storage within capacity in each time step (ac-ft)
  55      RivMassBal(seas)    River mass balance downstream of reservoir in each timestep (ac-ft)
  56      ResMassBal(seas)    Reservoir mass balance in each time step (ac-ft)
  57      BuildChoice(src)    Can only implement one project size;
  58   
  59   
  60  SupplyArea(seas)..       Area =L= SUM(src,V(src,seas))/Demand(seas);
  61  NetBen..                 TotalBen =E= Rev*Area - SUM(src,SUM(cap,CostCap(src,cap)*I(src,cap)) + SUM(seas,CostOpr(src)*V(src, seas)));
  62  PumpCap(seas)..          V("pump",seas) =L= sum(cap,MaxCap("pump",cap)*I("pump",cap));
  63  ResCap(seas)..           Stor(seas) =L= sum(cap,MaxCap("res",cap)*I("res",cap));
  64  RivMassBal(seas)..       V("pump",seas) =L= Flow(seas) + BaseFlow;
  65  ResMassBal(seas)..       Stor(seas) =E= Inflow(seas) - Flow(seas) - V("res",seas) + stor(seas-1)$(ord(seas) gt 1);
  66  BuildChoice(src)..       sum(Cap,I(src,cap)) =L= 1;
  67   
  68   
  69  Model BuildScenario /ALL/;
  70   
  71   
  72  Solve BuildScenario Using mip Maximizing TotalBen;
  73   
  74  Display V.L, I.L, TotalBen.L;
  75   
  76   
  77  Execute_Unload "Ex7-1.gdx";
  78   
  79  Execute "gdx2xls Ex7-1.gdx"
  80   


